WEBVTT

00:00:13.263 --> 00:00:15.265
[heart beating]

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:17.726
THE TRAITOR IS…

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:21.730
TSUZURA

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:22.981
Now, then.

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:25.233
For the second round,

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:27.277
all ten of you will play again.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.487
And we'll have you stay on the same teams.

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:31.948
-[girls gasping]
-What?

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.617
But didn't all of us here
get couple up last time?

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.120
-So why would--
-You're asking me why?

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.705
Isn't it obvious?

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.875
All of this amuses me.

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:45.253
I love seeing you all get confused
and panic like rats.

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:49.299
[alarm chiming]

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:51.676
Listen up, all!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.013
We'll open up second-round registration
for the next ten minutes.

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:58.808
To anyone that might be interested,
please come by the registration desk.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.019
All right.

00:01:03.021 --> 00:01:05.023
[Sachiko] If I found myself
in your position,

00:01:05.106 --> 00:01:07.609
I'd participate in a heartbeat.

00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:09.527
If you do nothing, aside from stand there,

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:11.654
you're doomed to become a house pet.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:13.990
You have ten minutes left.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.242
Think carefully about your next move.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.092
[Tsuzura] Mary?

00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:33.218
Huh?

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:39.808
I'm not gonna play
the second round.

00:01:39.891 --> 00:01:40.725
What?

00:01:41.684 --> 00:01:42.811
I'm dropping out.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:44.979
I'm done.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.983
TWIN

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:35.071
You're sitting out the next round?

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.115
What about the donation money we owe?

00:02:37.198 --> 00:02:39.617
I haven't gotten myself in too much debt.

00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:43.705
I can ask my parents to borrow some money
to try and get through this.

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:45.623
I just hope
they don't have an issue with that.

00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:47.208
But what about later?

00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:49.377
You said we need cash on-hand
to make money!

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.129
So how are we supposed to do that?

00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:52.630
Don't know.

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:54.132
Wait. You said…

00:02:54.215 --> 00:02:56.926
You told me
that the two of us were gonna be winners.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.762
If you're not going to gamble,
then how do we win this?

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.265
If you walk away,
what's going to happen to the den?

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.893
You'll lose everything
we've been working so hard for.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.648
[Mary] Sorry. But you guys really need
to stop depending on me.

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:14.652
The two of you got along fine
without me before, right?

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.406
Yukimi, you were able
to pay the donations on your own.

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:20.909
And, Tsuzura, your family is wealthy.

00:03:21.492 --> 00:03:22.744
I can't help you out anymore,

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:25.538
but if you're in that bad of a spot,
maybe you should ask Musubi.

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:28.666
He seems to really fancy you too.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.252
What? What are you talking about?

00:03:34.422 --> 00:03:35.882
[Kurumi laughing]

00:03:35.965 --> 00:03:38.676
You're so mean
you made her cry.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:40.929
No, Mary.

00:03:41.638 --> 00:03:43.139
What do you want?

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.057
Huh?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.187
I do not know how the results ended up
the way that they did today,

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:50.688
so I can't say sorry.

00:03:51.272 --> 00:03:52.398
But you…

00:03:52.482 --> 00:03:55.818
The Mary I thought I knew
would never give up because of this!

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.863
If she thought she was betrayed,
she wouldn't walk away!

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:00.949
You are so smart.

00:04:01.032 --> 00:04:03.952
You're strong, and you put your all
into everything you do.

00:04:04.035 --> 00:04:05.328
You never give up!

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.580
You always turn it around and win!

00:04:07.664 --> 00:04:09.582
I know this better than anyone.

00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:12.293
And I know you, Mary. This isn't you.

00:04:16.172 --> 00:04:18.132
[Mary] <i>God, that makes me cringe.</i>

00:04:18.216 --> 00:04:19.842
<i>I put in my all?</i>

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:23.596
<i>Yeah. Well, if you hadn't betrayed me,</i>
<i>then we would've won.</i>

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.099
<i>There had to have been a traitor.</i>

00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:31.020
There's another way.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:35.358
A completely different,
much simpler possibility.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.276
Huh?

00:04:37.485 --> 00:04:39.779
So, what do you think you'll end up doing?

00:04:39.862 --> 00:04:40.738
Huh?

00:04:40.822 --> 00:04:41.990
The second round.

00:04:42.073 --> 00:04:44.492
There's less
than five minutes left to register.

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.996
Oh, yeah. You're right.

00:04:48.496 --> 00:04:50.623
-I'll have to trust Tsuzura.
-Huh?

00:04:51.207 --> 00:04:52.625
I'll play in the second round.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:54.711
Do you mean that?

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.879
Tsuzura, thanks for that.

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:58.715
I'm thinking more clearly now.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:03.720
It's okay. I just really… Hmm?

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:07.932
It wouldn't be a good idea for me
to let you lose if you did betray me.

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:09.976
I want to be the one that beats you down.

00:05:12.061 --> 00:05:14.355
What? Hey!
Do you even know what you're saying?

00:05:14.439 --> 00:05:16.357
They're fighting.

00:05:16.441 --> 00:05:18.860
I want the three of you
to play in the second round too.

00:05:18.943 --> 00:05:20.278
I'm definitely in.

00:05:20.361 --> 00:05:23.489
There's no way I'd miss out
on something fun like this.

00:05:23.573 --> 00:05:26.492
Uh, I don't know what I should do.

00:05:26.576 --> 00:05:28.578
Well, if you want to you can quit now,

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.580
but, if you ask me,
it's a waste not to play.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:33.583
-Huh?
-We're definitely going to win.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.336
Come with me. I'll explain while we walk.

00:05:37.211 --> 00:05:40.340
But, uh,
I don't want you around when I do.

00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:43.051
Wait. What?
What's that supposed to mean?

00:05:49.891 --> 00:05:51.017
[Mary exhaling]

00:05:54.103 --> 00:05:56.105
Another simple strategy this time.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:59.734
We'll all pick a different guy
to confess to, just like we did before.

00:05:59.817 --> 00:06:02.612
Huh? So what would stop us
from losing this time around?

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.615
We lost the last game
because Tsuzura betrayed us

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:08.034
and told the guys
who we were confessing to.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:12.121
So let's do the same thing again,
but this time we'll leave Tsuzura out.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:15.750
Even with the four of us,
this strategy is still pretty effective.

00:06:15.833 --> 00:06:17.835
But even if she doesn't know
who we're going to pick,

00:06:17.919 --> 00:06:21.589
wouldn't Hanatemari still try
to pair herself up with someone anyway?

00:06:21.672 --> 00:06:24.133
I think there's a rule
that would make the second confessor lose

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.760
if she gets to him first.

00:06:25.843 --> 00:06:27.261
I wouldn't worry.

00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:28.304
Even if that did happen,

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:30.640
we'd still probably only end up
with one couple.

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.309
It's pretty unlikely
that out of the other three couples,

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.019
we'd end up with more than one.

00:06:35.103 --> 00:06:37.897
Even if something were to interfere
with those couplings,

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:41.401
we still have an advantage
from whatever benefit we want to declare.

00:06:41.484 --> 00:06:44.153
So regardless of what happens,
we can still end up winning.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:45.947
What are we winning though?

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.949
You're talking about money, right?

00:06:48.032 --> 00:06:49.367
Because these benefits…

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:51.786
I don't want to have to sleep
with someone that I don't know.

00:06:51.869 --> 00:06:53.663
I would rather die!

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:55.832
I'm sorry, Mary.

00:06:56.332 --> 00:06:58.501
You need
to find someone else for this team.

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:01.838
I'd prefer it
if we didn't change anyone out.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.715
If the person they swapped you with
ended up being a plant by the guys,

00:07:04.799 --> 00:07:05.800
it'd be a disaster.

00:07:07.969 --> 00:07:11.973
Yukimi, you care about
that gambling den just as much as we do.

00:07:12.515 --> 00:07:14.934
If you give up now,
you give up everything.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.355
You have to take on risk
to get what you want.

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:21.774
Isn't that the core of what gambling is?

00:07:28.739 --> 00:07:31.159
Here. I'm giving you the gambling den.

00:07:31.242 --> 00:07:33.536
-This should be enough to prove it.
-Huh?

00:07:37.373 --> 00:07:38.791
…TRANSFER TO YUKIMI TOGAKUSHI

00:07:38.875 --> 00:07:41.669
That transfer request should
at least let you keep the den

00:07:41.752 --> 00:07:43.004
even if you lose, right?

00:07:43.504 --> 00:07:46.799
Ugh. Fine! I guess I'll play again.

00:07:46.883 --> 00:07:48.634
Okay. What about you two?

00:07:48.718 --> 00:07:51.220
Oh, I'm in. Let's get this done!

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:54.056
We've come this far,
so I'll see it through until the end.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.600
Happy to hear it.

00:07:55.683 --> 00:07:57.810
Do you know where I can get a lineup card?

00:07:57.894 --> 00:07:59.353
Oh, I have one.

00:07:59.437 --> 00:08:01.314
It's an extra from before.

00:08:01.397 --> 00:08:03.274
Let me take care of the details.

00:08:03.357 --> 00:08:05.943
I already know what we should do.
I have a plan.

00:08:06.027 --> 00:08:07.153
Okay.

00:08:08.905 --> 00:08:11.115
Take a look
and remember your picks.

00:08:11.199 --> 00:08:13.451
I have to pick Musubi again?

00:08:13.534 --> 00:08:15.161
Why these couples, specifically?

00:08:15.244 --> 00:08:16.704
That's a secret.

00:08:16.787 --> 00:08:17.622
Wait a minute.

00:08:17.705 --> 00:08:20.458
If we're gonna be on the same team,
shouldn't we at least know why?

00:08:21.083 --> 00:08:22.585
<i>This is amusing.</i>

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:25.963
<i>Saotome may be saying Hanatemari</i>
<i>is the traitor,</i>

00:08:26.047 --> 00:08:29.717
<i>but in reality,</i>
<i>I don't think she trusts anybody here.</i>

00:08:30.635 --> 00:08:34.805
<i>I assume that's why she put herself last,</i>
<i>since it's the safest position.</i>

00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:37.725
<i>It allows her to avoid</i>
<i>doubling up with anyone.</i>

00:08:38.392 --> 00:08:42.522
<i>She sensed her power within the group</i>
<i>and naturally made herself our leader.</i>

00:08:42.605 --> 00:08:45.066
<i>What a fiendishly clever woman.</i>

00:08:47.068 --> 00:08:48.986
<i>Oh, this is fun.</i>

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.280
<i>There's just over three minutes left</i>
<i>to register.</i>

00:08:51.364 --> 00:08:53.658
<i>So, please get those cards in!</i>

00:08:53.741 --> 00:08:57.119
We're following your lead.
Have any ideas for round two, Chief?

00:08:57.203 --> 00:08:59.914
I don't. I think I might be done, guys.

00:08:59.997 --> 00:09:03.251
I don't see the point.
Hanatemari doesn't seem like she likes me.

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:06.629
And I don't think Togakushi
likes me either.

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:07.922
I don't stand a chance.

00:09:08.005 --> 00:09:11.008
Even if I did take her to dinner,
I don't think things would change.

00:09:11.092 --> 00:09:13.844
Ugh. Why did I ever care
about this stupid game?

00:09:13.928 --> 00:09:17.765
Besides, it's not like we can just do
the same thing again.

00:09:17.848 --> 00:09:20.393
Uh, I can't argue with that, but…

00:09:20.476 --> 00:09:23.020
Maybe we should call it quits.

00:09:23.104 --> 00:09:26.274
Hey. What are you doing, Haruto?

00:09:26.357 --> 00:09:28.818
This is a game
we're guaranteed to win if we play.

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:31.779
Stopping at 330,000 isn't enough for me.

00:09:31.862 --> 00:09:34.031
Hey. You don't need to convince me.

00:09:34.115 --> 00:09:36.701
Then maybe you should be putting in
a little more effort

00:09:36.784 --> 00:09:40.037
Even if we do end up losing, this patsy's
gonna cover our entrance fees.

00:09:41.998 --> 00:09:43.082
Hmm?

00:09:43.165 --> 00:09:45.042
Looks like good news is on the way.

00:09:45.126 --> 00:09:48.421
All right, you guys. I just found out
who the girls are confessing to.

00:09:48.504 --> 00:09:49.422
Huh?

00:09:49.505 --> 00:09:51.424
Oh, hell yeah. So?

00:09:51.507 --> 00:09:53.050
They finished talking it over,

00:09:53.134 --> 00:09:55.553
and our friend let me know
who everyone's gonna pick.

00:09:55.636 --> 00:09:57.388
Sweet! That's lucky.

00:09:57.471 --> 00:09:59.432
Chief, let's get in on this next round.

00:09:59.515 --> 00:10:00.641
Uh…

00:10:01.142 --> 00:10:03.853
Money wasn't really the reason
I was playing this.

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:05.938
I heard something
that might interest you.

00:10:06.522 --> 00:10:07.732
You know Togakushi?

00:10:07.815 --> 00:10:10.693
She's picking you.
She wants to offer a "sleep over."

00:10:10.776 --> 00:10:12.695
You sure about that?

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.739
Sounds like good news for you, Chief.

00:10:14.822 --> 00:10:17.742
So if you play the next round,
you'll definitely get some!

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:21.621
[Musubi exclaiming]

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.753
[MC] <i>All right, everyone!</i>

00:10:28.836 --> 00:10:31.839
<i>Registration for the second round</i>
<i>is now closed!</i>

00:10:35.718 --> 00:10:38.638
[Tsuzura groaning]

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:41.891
[MC] <i>Let's get started!</i>

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:44.810
This is the final round,
so prepare yourselves.

00:10:44.894 --> 00:10:47.521
Are you ready? Let's get coupling!

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:51.025
Round two begins now!

00:10:53.861 --> 00:10:55.613
Does everybody remember the plan?

00:10:55.696 --> 00:10:57.281
I don't want any surprises.

00:10:57.865 --> 00:10:58.699
Got it!

00:10:58.783 --> 00:11:02.370
Is it a good idea for us
to talk about it right here?

00:11:02.453 --> 00:11:05.331
It's fine.
This is game will be ours to take.

00:11:05.414 --> 00:11:07.291
We were destined to become winners.

00:11:09.126 --> 00:11:12.296
Very well.
Are there any benefits to declare?

00:11:13.255 --> 00:11:15.800
I'm not afraid of risking anything to win.

00:11:15.883 --> 00:11:17.927
"Sleep over" please.

00:11:18.636 --> 00:11:19.804
Anyone else?

00:11:20.513 --> 00:11:21.806
Yeah. Me too.

00:11:24.141 --> 00:11:26.769
Two participants for "sleep over."

00:11:26.852 --> 00:11:28.562
-Uh, um…
-Yes?

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:30.314
I wanna…

00:11:30.398 --> 00:11:32.483
If you're serious
about wanting to be a winner,

00:11:32.566 --> 00:11:34.360
then you should be taking
the biggest risk.

00:11:34.443 --> 00:11:38.155
But, you know, I guess none of that
would matter to a traitor, would it?

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.619
I'll do it! I'll offer a "sleep over!"

00:11:46.831 --> 00:11:49.041
Wow. This is getting intense.

00:11:49.125 --> 00:11:50.251
Y'all are fricking horny.

00:11:50.334 --> 00:11:52.169
Thank you. Noted.

00:11:52.253 --> 00:11:53.754
Please begin the next round.

00:11:53.838 --> 00:11:55.756
I'll start us off!

00:11:58.467 --> 00:12:01.804
Hey, Chief! I know Hanatemari
is the girl you like better,

00:12:01.887 --> 00:12:03.180
but if you choose Togakushi,

00:12:03.264 --> 00:12:05.057
you'll probably be able
to get to third base.

00:12:05.141 --> 00:12:06.475
Just think about this.

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:08.269
Yeah. I'm trying to, man.

00:12:08.352 --> 00:12:10.146
CIRCLE THE OBJECT OF YOUR AFFECTION

00:12:10.229 --> 00:12:13.315
<i>I was surprised</i>
<i>when she wanted us to play again.</i>

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:16.402
<i>Hard to believe you'd get different</i>
<i>results from the same members, really.</i>

00:12:17.111 --> 00:12:21.157
<i>Does Saotome have some sort of vendetta</i>
<i>against Juraku and the Student Council?</i>

00:12:21.741 --> 00:12:24.201
<i>But the worst-case scenario</i>
<i>didn't happen.</i>

00:12:24.285 --> 00:12:27.121
<i>Saotome abandoned Hanatemari</i>
<i>for betraying her trust,</i>

00:12:27.204 --> 00:12:31.542
<i>so it makes sense to share</i>
<i>who we'll confess to among the four of us,</i>

00:12:31.625 --> 00:12:33.878
<i>without Hanatemari.</i>

00:12:33.961 --> 00:12:37.298
<i>But unfortunately for Mary,</i>
<i>that plan is already a bust.</i>

00:12:37.882 --> 00:12:39.216
<i>You know why?</i>

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:42.178
<i>Because I'm the one who betrayed them!</i>

00:12:42.261 --> 00:12:44.054
Okay. I've made my choice.

00:12:44.138 --> 00:12:46.307
YES/NO

00:12:47.725 --> 00:12:51.312
[Chitose] <i>Musubi is the heir</i>
<i>to a filthy-rich, corporate CEO.</i>

00:12:51.395 --> 00:12:54.523
<i>He and his four little doggies begged me</i>
<i>to help them get some girls</i>

00:12:54.607 --> 00:12:56.317
<i>in return for some cash.</i>

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:00.446
<i>Musubi is rich,</i>
<i>but money doesn't make up for who he is.</i>

00:13:00.529 --> 00:13:02.865
<i>He's obsessed with women</i>
<i>who present themselves</i>

00:13:02.948 --> 00:13:05.451
<i>with stereotypical ideas of femininity.</i>

00:13:05.534 --> 00:13:08.454
<i>He's playing this game to take</i>
<i>advantage of the "benefits."</i>

00:13:09.163 --> 00:13:12.541
<i>To be honest,</i>
<i>he really kinda makes my skin crawl.</i>

00:13:13.167 --> 00:13:15.461
<i>Well,</i>
<i>it's not like I have to deal with him,</i>

00:13:15.544 --> 00:13:18.589
<i>so I'm just gonna keep focusing</i>
<i>on getting paid.</i>

00:13:18.672 --> 00:13:21.509
<i>I mean, wouldn't it be a waste</i>
<i>to claw my way into this school</i>

00:13:21.592 --> 00:13:24.220
<i>and not make any money once I got here?</i>

00:13:24.303 --> 00:13:26.222
<i>Sorry for selling you out,</i>

00:13:26.305 --> 00:13:28.974
<i>but I hope you enjoy those benefits.</i>

00:13:29.058 --> 00:13:31.018
Which of you would like to start?

00:13:31.101 --> 00:13:32.311
Oh, right.

00:13:32.394 --> 00:13:34.480
I'm confessing to Sera.

00:13:34.563 --> 00:13:37.483
But just for this round.
I'm doing this for the sake of the game.

00:13:37.566 --> 00:13:40.486
Kuonji's still the only man
that has my heart!

00:13:40.569 --> 00:13:42.863
Great. Next confession. Go ahead.

00:13:42.947 --> 00:13:44.698
Oh, that would be me.

00:13:45.199 --> 00:13:48.494
So let's just see here.

00:13:48.577 --> 00:13:52.414
<i>The guys paid me real well</i>
<i>to know who's confessing to whom.</i>

00:13:53.082 --> 00:13:54.500
<i>Other than Hanatemari,</i>

00:13:54.583 --> 00:13:57.753
<i>everyone else is practically guaranteed</i>
<i>to become a couple.</i>

00:13:57.837 --> 00:14:01.757
<i>Those idiots would probably suspect me</i>
<i>if I didn't pair up with someone too.</i>

00:14:01.841 --> 00:14:03.509
Your confession, Kurume.

00:14:03.592 --> 00:14:06.762
Boom! I confess to Kuonji right now!

00:14:08.222 --> 00:14:10.057
But are you sure, Kurume?

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.351
What happened
to us all following the plan?

00:14:12.434 --> 00:14:14.520
Huh? Why would I worry about that?

00:14:14.603 --> 00:14:18.065
Didn't Mary tell us flat-out
one of us was a traitor?

00:14:18.148 --> 00:14:21.151
It wouldn't make much sense
to follow the plan now, would it?

00:14:21.735 --> 00:14:23.654
I guess not.

00:14:24.238 --> 00:14:27.116
<i>Don't give me that look!</i>
<i>It's not my fault!</i>

00:14:27.199 --> 00:14:28.284
Next person.

00:14:28.367 --> 00:14:31.203
Me next. I gotta make my choice.

00:14:31.287 --> 00:14:33.789
<i>Togakushi followed through</i>
<i>in the first round.</i>

00:14:33.873 --> 00:14:35.499
<i>She should stick with the plan.</i>

00:14:43.632 --> 00:14:45.426
[Musubi] <i>The road has been long.</i>

00:14:45.926 --> 00:14:47.177
<i>Looking back, </i>

00:14:47.261 --> 00:14:52.099
<i>all 17 years of my life have been filled</i>
<i>with rejection from girls.</i>

00:14:52.182 --> 00:14:55.102
<i>I'd tell them my feelings</i>
<i>and get shot down.</i>

00:14:55.853 --> 00:15:00.232
<i>Sometimes they wouldn't even talk to me</i>
<i>because I creep them out.</i>

00:15:01.567 --> 00:15:03.944
<i>But all of that is coming to an end.</i>

00:15:04.028 --> 00:15:05.738
<i>Today I become a man!</i>

00:15:07.615 --> 00:15:09.909
Are you ready? I need your confession.

00:15:09.992 --> 00:15:10.910
Yes.

00:15:10.993 --> 00:15:13.537
<i>I'll win this game</i>
<i>and "sleep over"!</i>

00:15:13.621 --> 00:15:15.289
<i>I can't wait to get paid.</i>

00:15:15.372 --> 00:15:17.791
All right. I'm making my confession now.

00:15:17.875 --> 00:15:21.754
<i>This is it! I win!</i>

00:15:23.339 --> 00:15:25.257
I'm choosing Kibashira.

00:15:28.302 --> 00:15:29.261
Why me?

00:15:30.095 --> 00:15:32.014
<i>What? Not possible.</i>

00:15:32.097 --> 00:15:34.350
<i>Is Togakushi betraying Saotome too?</i>

00:15:35.351 --> 00:15:36.977
Next confession, please.

00:15:37.061 --> 00:15:38.103
Oh, that's me.

00:15:38.604 --> 00:15:40.731
<i>Dammit. What the hell is going on?</i>

00:15:40.814 --> 00:15:44.860
<i>This cow gave up on Hanatemari,</i>
<i>and chose Togakushi to be safe.</i>

00:15:44.944 --> 00:15:45.861
<i>If they don't pair up,</i>

00:15:45.945 --> 00:15:48.238
<i>we're gonna walk away from this</i>
<i>with empty pockets.</i>

00:15:48.322 --> 00:15:49.865
Hanatemari?

00:15:52.076 --> 00:15:53.702
Here goes nothing.

00:15:53.786 --> 00:15:55.245
I think I'm gonna pick…

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:57.748
I confess to Musubi.

00:15:59.333 --> 00:16:03.504
[Ren] <i>Musubi made it pretty fricking clear</i>
<i>that he was into Hanatemari first round!</i>

00:16:03.587 --> 00:16:06.090
<i>Why would she take such a big risk</i>
<i>by picking him?</i>

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.968
Wow, Musubi.

00:16:09.843 --> 00:16:12.721
I didn't realize
you were such a popular guy.

00:16:12.805 --> 00:16:15.516
I think I might be jealous.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:20.729
[Mary] 'Cause I'm madly
in love with you too.

00:16:26.819 --> 00:16:30.572
Thank you. This concludes round two
of the coupling game.

00:16:30.656 --> 00:16:33.742
There's only been one successful pairing
at this table.

00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:36.203
Congratulations to Inui and Sera.

00:16:36.286 --> 00:16:38.122
Best wishes for you both.

00:16:38.205 --> 00:16:40.207
This can't be. I did…

00:16:41.041 --> 00:16:43.585
You're more stupid than I thought.

00:16:43.669 --> 00:16:47.589
Inui, your little game to betray us
wasn't as clever as you hoped.

00:16:47.673 --> 00:16:49.883
Th…that's not the truth.

00:16:49.967 --> 00:16:51.301
I didn't do anything.

00:16:51.385 --> 00:16:54.471
Come on.
You don't need to play dumb anymore.

00:16:54.555 --> 00:16:57.349
I have been keeping a close eye
on everything you've done.

00:16:57.433 --> 00:16:58.559
In the first round,

00:16:58.642 --> 00:17:01.729
Tsuzura was the only person
who knew who I was confessing to,

00:17:01.812 --> 00:17:05.107
but somehow,
everyone still got coupled up anyway.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.692
That really threw me off.

00:17:06.775 --> 00:17:10.529
The only logical conclusion was
that Tsuzura had snuck you our choices.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.365
But there was something about it
that didn't add up.

00:17:13.449 --> 00:17:15.909
Tsuzura would never betray me.

00:17:15.993 --> 00:17:19.246
Everything else started falling into place
when I remembered that.

00:17:19.329 --> 00:17:20.748
Oh, Mary!

00:17:20.831 --> 00:17:24.668
Honestly, it was easy to tell
something was off right from the start.

00:17:24.752 --> 00:17:26.503
I'm sure I wasn't the only one who noticed

00:17:26.587 --> 00:17:29.923
that the dealer never said
any of our names out loud during the game.

00:17:30.007 --> 00:17:31.592
Next person, please.

00:17:31.675 --> 00:17:32.801
Next lady, please.

00:17:32.885 --> 00:17:34.136
Next player.

00:17:34.219 --> 00:17:37.389
So I started going back through
all the events of the day in my head,

00:17:37.473 --> 00:17:39.558
and that's when I remembered something.

00:17:39.641 --> 00:17:41.769
Specifically, the use of the lineup cards.

00:17:41.852 --> 00:17:43.395
The cards?

00:17:43.479 --> 00:17:44.938
Think about it.

00:17:45.022 --> 00:17:46.065
In the first round,

00:17:46.148 --> 00:17:49.651
all of us sat at the table in the order
we'd written down on that card.

00:17:49.735 --> 00:17:52.988
And that corresponded to when we needed
to make our confessions too,

00:17:53.072 --> 00:17:56.158
because we all assumed our names
were in the order we'd all agreed on.

00:17:56.742 --> 00:17:57.868
Mm… mm-hmm.

00:17:57.951 --> 00:17:59.161
But hear me out.

00:17:59.244 --> 00:18:02.247
What if whoever wrote the order
of our names on the lineup card

00:18:02.331 --> 00:18:04.833
had actually slid them
one position forward?

00:18:04.917 --> 00:18:05.751
Huh.

00:18:05.834 --> 00:18:07.044
Hang on a second.

00:18:07.127 --> 00:18:10.089
So even if we were confessing
in our seated order,

00:18:10.172 --> 00:18:13.759
the number assigned to the confessor
on the chart belonged to someone else.

00:18:14.426 --> 00:18:16.887
So before we got to say
who we were picking,

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.931
those cheaters
would have already seen the card

00:18:19.014 --> 00:18:21.058
and known who we were confessing to.

00:18:21.141 --> 00:18:22.309
SELECT GIRL #2? YES

00:18:22.392 --> 00:18:23.894
Juraku told us…

00:18:24.645 --> 00:18:27.064
"No house staff has altered your results."

00:18:27.147 --> 00:18:28.565
The house didn't cheat,

00:18:28.649 --> 00:18:31.318
but that doesn't mean
they didn't endorse who did.

00:18:31.401 --> 00:18:33.278
The dealer would have seen it coming.

00:18:33.362 --> 00:18:35.697
To the rest of us,
it wouldn't have been as obvious.

00:18:35.781 --> 00:18:39.493
The con fell apart once that piece
of the puzzle fell into place.

00:18:39.576 --> 00:18:41.328
One person would have that opportunity.

00:18:41.411 --> 00:18:44.498
And Inui had volunteered
to submit the lineup card.

00:18:44.581 --> 00:18:47.084
But you know what they say
about hindsight being 20/20.

00:18:47.167 --> 00:18:50.129
So, I wrote everything down myself
the second round.

00:18:50.212 --> 00:18:52.339
I didn't want to give Inui another chance.

00:18:52.422 --> 00:18:53.549
Well played.

00:18:53.632 --> 00:18:56.343
But Inui wouldn't have used
the same trick twice.

00:18:56.426 --> 00:18:58.971
The second round
was a much simpler con, wasn't it?

00:18:59.555 --> 00:19:01.223
Signaling.

00:19:01.306 --> 00:19:03.851
You can use your smartphone or body tells.

00:19:03.934 --> 00:19:05.727
It doesn't matter which, really.

00:19:05.811 --> 00:19:08.730
Getting the correct information
communicated discreetly to the men

00:19:08.814 --> 00:19:09.731
isn't difficult.

00:19:09.815 --> 00:19:11.233
So tell me, Mary.

00:19:11.316 --> 00:19:13.610
How did you overcome these circumstances?

00:19:13.694 --> 00:19:17.364
You don't know?
I think that was the easiest part.

00:19:17.447 --> 00:19:20.576
It wasn't a con,
I just never really doubted these three.

00:19:21.577 --> 00:19:22.995
[Sachiko] Hmm?

00:19:23.579 --> 00:19:25.414
I hadn't met Kurume before,

00:19:25.497 --> 00:19:28.500
so I had every reason
to suspect her being the traitor.

00:19:28.584 --> 00:19:31.503
We never had a chance
to establish mutual trust.

00:19:31.587 --> 00:19:33.338
So I decided to roll with that.

00:19:33.839 --> 00:19:36.049
If she was the traitor,
I could gamble that.

00:19:36.133 --> 00:19:38.135
And if she wasn't, she could assume I was.

00:19:38.218 --> 00:19:40.888
I just banked on the fact
that she was an unstable element.

00:19:40.971 --> 00:19:43.932
I mean, we've never interacted
with each other before.

00:19:44.016 --> 00:19:44.933
With that said,

00:19:45.017 --> 00:19:48.145
I figured she would probably change up
her answer at the last minute.

00:19:48.228 --> 00:19:50.981
She has absolutely no reason to trust me,

00:19:51.064 --> 00:19:53.025
so I just trusted in that.

00:19:53.108 --> 00:19:54.651
Well, aren't you clever?

00:19:54.735 --> 00:19:57.237
So, it was lucky that I changed my mind.

00:19:58.405 --> 00:20:01.408
When it came to Yukimi,
I signaled the plan in writing.

00:20:01.491 --> 00:20:04.203
I had to trust
that she had my best interests at heart,

00:20:04.286 --> 00:20:07.789
and that if I needed her to do something,
she would most likely pull it off.

00:20:07.873 --> 00:20:09.917
No way! The transfer!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:13.503
Yep. I left her a clue
when I wrote down our transfer.

00:20:13.587 --> 00:20:15.505
If you weren't paying attention,

00:20:15.589 --> 00:20:18.508
my show of giving her the rights
to the den must have been convincing,

00:20:18.592 --> 00:20:20.969
but the name of the den
that I wrote was a fake one.

00:20:21.053 --> 00:20:22.387
Not the one that we use.

00:20:22.471 --> 00:20:26.183
I tried to consider all the reasons
why Saotome would do something like that,

00:20:26.266 --> 00:20:28.310
and I chose to believe
that it was a message to me

00:20:28.393 --> 00:20:30.145
that she was putting on an act.

00:20:30.229 --> 00:20:32.773
So I decided to change
who I was confessing to.

00:20:34.316 --> 00:20:35.901
What about Hanatemari, then?

00:20:35.984 --> 00:20:38.528
She didn't have a chance
to hear any of our plan!

00:20:39.529 --> 00:20:42.115
I was feeling so alone and confused,

00:20:42.199 --> 00:20:44.451
but I always end up
being a problem eventually,

00:20:44.534 --> 00:20:46.745
so I figured
this was just how it would end.

00:20:47.246 --> 00:20:50.415
I needed Mary to remind me
about the promise we made together.

00:20:52.876 --> 00:20:54.920
This game will be ours to take.

00:20:55.003 --> 00:20:57.047
We were destined to become winners.

00:20:57.631 --> 00:21:01.426
She's amazing.
Mary risked so much to send the message.

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:04.179
But that's what you have to do
if you want to win.

00:21:04.763 --> 00:21:08.433
Today, I made sure
I only took time to speak with Musubi.

00:21:09.017 --> 00:21:12.229
It was obvious that choosing Musubi
posed the greatest risk to me

00:21:12.312 --> 00:21:13.522
of being paired up.

00:21:14.273 --> 00:21:15.691
I didn't care.

00:21:15.774 --> 00:21:17.484
That was the gamble I made.

00:21:17.985 --> 00:21:20.779
What? I don't get this at all!

00:21:20.862 --> 00:21:23.615
All of these are just vague,
random references.

00:21:23.699 --> 00:21:26.618
What kind of relationship
do you two have that makes this possible?

00:21:27.661 --> 00:21:29.538
<i>It's funny you can't guess.</i>

00:21:30.914 --> 00:21:34.001
<i>Mary is my Prince Charming!</i>

00:21:36.837 --> 00:21:38.630
[Chitose shuddering]

00:21:40.215 --> 00:21:42.175
Well, that about wraps it up.

00:21:42.259 --> 00:21:44.928
Long story short,
I saw right through your little setup

00:21:45.012 --> 00:21:46.638
and you all walked into my trap.

00:21:46.722 --> 00:21:49.391
You said the wager was doubled
this time around, right?

00:21:50.475 --> 00:21:52.519
I should thank you and your colleagues.

00:21:52.602 --> 00:21:54.980
You were easy to beat.

00:21:55.063 --> 00:21:57.524
Now I have so much money.

00:21:57.607 --> 00:21:59.109
Thank you, boys.

00:21:59.192 --> 00:22:00.485
Say that again!

00:22:00.569 --> 00:22:03.572
Can you please stop provoking them
when we're about to close?

00:22:03.655 --> 00:22:05.365
We don't have time to deal with anger.

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:09.870
Your wagers will be collected by
the Beautification and Makeover Committee,

00:22:09.953 --> 00:22:11.705
and delivered promptly to you.

00:22:11.788 --> 00:22:13.707
The benefits are at your discretion.

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:16.376
If they are not executed,
please contact us.

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:18.253
Table three is now complete.

00:22:18.837 --> 00:22:22.674
Okay. The final table
has turned in their confessions.

00:22:22.758 --> 00:22:25.844
That about wraps up everything
we have on the schedule.

00:22:26.345 --> 00:22:30.140
<i>We hope you had a great time</i>
<i>at today's Coupling Party.</i>

00:22:30.223 --> 00:22:33.602
<i>The results from this event are always</i>
<i>wildly different from group to group,</i>

00:22:33.685 --> 00:22:36.521
<i>but whether you leave here today alone</i>
<i>or with a partner,</i>

00:22:36.605 --> 00:22:39.232
<i>we always try to make sure</i>
<i>we have fun!</i>

00:22:39.316 --> 00:22:40.442
<i>Thanks so much!</i>

00:22:40.525 --> 00:22:44.321
<i>The 50th Annual Coupling Party</i>
<i>is now officially over! </i>

00:22:45.113 --> 00:22:47.824
<i>We hope to see you singles</i>
<i>at the 51st one! </i>

00:22:47.908 --> 00:22:49.368
<i>Take care, everybody!</i>

00:22:51.453 --> 00:22:55.248
[Aoi chuckling] She made a two million
comeback in the second round.

00:22:55.332 --> 00:22:58.043
Fantastic. I knew she could pull it off.

00:22:58.543 --> 00:23:00.253
You're going to let her join?

00:23:00.337 --> 00:23:02.422
Yeah. That's okay, right?

00:23:03.215 --> 00:23:06.760
Something tells me we'll want
to keep Mary real close to the chest.

00:23:07.928 --> 00:23:10.013
For our plan to work, she's necessary.

00:23:12.015 --> 00:23:14.893
Wow. I wasn't sure
how that was gonna play out.

00:23:14.976 --> 00:23:17.312
I'm glad we managed to pull through
in the end, though.

00:23:17.396 --> 00:23:19.356
Yeah. You're so right.

00:23:19.439 --> 00:23:21.274
We couldn't have done it without Mary.

00:23:21.358 --> 00:23:22.776
-Hey, you guys.
-Huh?

00:23:22.859 --> 00:23:24.277
Please forgive me.

00:23:24.361 --> 00:23:26.321
Whoa. Wait. What's wrong?

00:23:26.947 --> 00:23:27.781
I just…

00:23:27.864 --> 00:23:31.159
I questioned your integrity
when it really mattered.

00:23:31.243 --> 00:23:34.037
The two of you didn't do anything
to deserve that.

00:23:34.621 --> 00:23:37.374
-I'm sorry!
-What? No. Don't worry about it.

00:23:37.457 --> 00:23:40.293
No one could blame you
after the con they tried to pull.

00:23:40.377 --> 00:23:43.213
And, hey, it all worked out in the end,
so let's consider--

00:23:46.383 --> 00:23:47.801
I was scared.

00:23:48.385 --> 00:23:52.389
I keep feeling like I've been holding
you back from being your best.

00:23:52.472 --> 00:23:54.683
I thought you wanted to get rid of me.

00:23:56.143 --> 00:23:59.312
[Mary] I don't know what I would do
if that happened, Mary.

00:24:02.107 --> 00:24:04.443
[Mary] You taught me something
very important today.

00:24:05.026 --> 00:24:07.946
It's important
to believe in the people around me.

00:24:10.031 --> 00:24:12.325
Yeah. I know it sounds really cheesy,

00:24:12.409 --> 00:24:15.620
but we only won because I knew
the two of you would have my back.

00:24:15.704 --> 00:24:17.122
And you guys knew me well enough

00:24:17.205 --> 00:24:19.583
to trust
that I would never leave you behind.

00:24:20.625 --> 00:24:22.335
Oh, come on. I'm blushing.

00:24:26.548 --> 00:24:29.009
Thank you so much for believing in me.

00:24:30.802 --> 00:24:32.345
Let's make a promise.

00:24:32.429 --> 00:24:35.474
We'll never let anyone
get between the three of us again.

00:24:36.850 --> 00:24:37.684
Yeah!

00:24:41.062 --> 00:24:43.064
[ending theme music playing]

00:26:11.069 --> 00:26:13.071
[orchestral music playing]

00:26:25.083 --> 00:26:26.042
[dishes clattering]
